The confirmation rate of a user is the number of 'confirmed' messages divided by the total number of requested confirmation messages. 
The confirmation rate of a user that did not request any confirmation messages is 0. Round the confirmation rate to two decimal places.

Write a solution to find the confirmation rate of each user.

Return the result table in any order.


SOLUTION:

SELECT Signups.user_id, 
COALESCE(ROUND(SUM(IF(Confirmations.action = 'confirmed', 1, 0)) / COUNT(Confirmations.action),2), 0) AS confirmation_rate 
-- coalesce for if null, IF isn't specifically necessary but can aid readability when understanding logic
FROM Signups LEFT JOIN Confirmations -- LEFT JOIN ensures all user_id are conserved for when 0% confirmation_rate is necessary
ON Signups.user_id = Confirmations.user_id
GROUP BY Signups.user_id
